# The corpus data blob lives in the S3 corpus remote (content-addressed,
# add-only) and only the small `corpus.db.ref` pointer (written by
# `fedcourts corpus-push`) is committed to git. Never commit the blob itself,
# its download staging file, or its SQLite sidecar files.
/corpus.db
/corpus.db.partial
/corpus.db-wal
/corpus.db-shm
# The pull's provenance sidecar: which pointer the blob on disk actually came
# from (written by `fedcourts corpus-pull`), so a blob pulled through the
# out-of-band override can never masquerade as the committed pointer's.
/corpus.db.pulled.ref
*.parquet
/index.db
corpus.db\?*
# The staging-corpus slice `corpus-seed-slice` builds here by default, and the
# pointer it publishes beside it: both are runner-local working files naming a
# non-production remote, and neither belongs in the repository.
/staging-slice.db
/staging-slice.db.ref
/staging-slice.db-wal
/staging-slice.db-shm
